<a target="_new" href="
http://www.womengamers.com/dw/shodan.htm">System Shock's Shodan Review</a><br>
Women Gamers&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
5/24/2002 6:07:34 AM<P>
WG member Irony reviews the female lead character Shodan of the System Shock and System Shock II games.<p>
"... SHODAN has the most positive attitude of any digital woman. She faces setback after setback - marooned on a planet in the middle of deep space, thwarted by both her creator and her own offspring, and hamstrung by a turncoat little cyborg - with aplomb, never losing her cool. She just finds a workaround every time. That's gumption." <br>
<hr>
<a href="reviews/173
">Look at you hacker, a pathetic creature of meat and bone...</a><br>
Wewp!&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
8/21/1999 11:04:58 AM<P>
Everyone remembers Wolfenstein 3D, and Doom. What most people don't remember is a game that had better control, better graphics options and gasp, dare I say it, a story! Not some slapped on affair, but a real plot with subplots and a logical progression. Sure, the masses are only interested in finding the gold key so they can get the next big gun to kill the next boss to get to the next level. But, for a few of us, that got tired after 2 such games. System Shock was the answer to our question, "How about an FPS that has some depth?"<br>
